From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMANET Firmware <noreply@openmanet.local>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] morse_driver: accept NDP ADDBA as AMPDU capability proof

Mesh peer capability parsing can leave ampdu_supported clear even when the
peer advertises and actively requests NDP Block Ack. That makes the driver's
RX_START callback return -EINVAL, which mac80211 reports to the peer as status
37. A valid NDP RX_START request directly proves the peer supports A-MPDU, so
repair the cached peer flag before applying the normal capability check. The
global enable_ampdu setting remains authoritative.
---
 .../patches/011-accept-ndp-addba-peer-capability.patch | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/feeds/morse/essentials/morse_driver/patches/011-accept-ndp-addba-peer-capability.patch b/feeds/morse/essentials/morse_driver/patches/011-accept-ndp-addba-peer-capability.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/feeds/morse/essentials/morse_driver/patches/011-accept-ndp-addba-peer-capability.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+--- a/mac.c
++++ b/mac.c
+@@ -4610,6 +4610,17 @@ morse_mac_ops_ampdu_action(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
+ 		return -EINVAL;
+ 	}
+ 
++#if defined(MORSE_MAC80211_S1G_FEATURE_NDP_BLOCKACK)
++	/* A valid NDP ADDBA request is direct evidence that this peer supports
++	 * A-MPDU. Repair mesh peers whose cached S1G capability was incomplete. */
++	if (params->ndp && action == IEEE80211_AMPDU_RX_START &&
++	    !mors_sta->ampdu_supported) {
++		MORSE_WARN(mors, "%s %pM.%d enabling AMPDU from NDP ADDBA request\n",
++			   __func__, mors_sta->addr, tid);
++		mors_sta->ampdu_supported = true;
++	}
++#endif
++
+ 	if (!mors_sta->ampdu_supported) {
+ 		MORSE_DBG(mors, "%s %pM.%d Denying AMPDU because STA doesn't support it\n",
+ 			  __func__, mors_sta->addr, tid);
-- 
2.50.1
